                     </biblList>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_beca52a5">
                        <head xml:id="head_6e074023">Evidence</head>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm147">"Ahasverus" occupied Hans Christian Andersen's mind for many years. In December 1844 he published "Fragmenter af H.C. Andersen's 'Ahasverus'", but Hartmann must have used Andersen's manuscript as his text source since he end-dated his original score on 20 February 1844. The complete poem was published in 1848. Why Hartmann decided to finish the composition as late as in 1875 is not known.</p>
            </history>
